It is late Friday evening.
Before we go to bed, I take Ludwig out.
We go for a short walk in the neighborhood.
The streets are very quiet now.
Ludwig walks nicely next to me.
Suddenly he stops.
He sniffs eagerly at something on the pavement.
It is a dirty bag with food scraps.
He opens his mouth to take it.
"No, drop it!" I say firmly to him.
I gently pull him away from the bag.
"The trash is not food, Ludwig," I explain.
"Come here, Ludwig," I call to him.
He drops the bag and looks up at me.
He quickly begins to wag his tail.
"Good boy," I say and pet him.
We continue our walk down the street.
Now we just need to go home and sleep.
